1
00:00:00,041 --> 00:00:00,041
25.000

2
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:26,693
No common failure,

3
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:33,033
whether it be sickness or bankruptcy
or professional misfortune,

4
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:38,496
will reverberate so cruelly and deeply
in the unconscious as a divorce,

5
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:44,586
It penetrates the seat of all anguish,

6
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,380
forcing it to life,

7
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:54,804
With one cut, it slices more deeply
than life can ever reach,

8
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:34,761
FAITHLESS

9
00:01:57,492 --> 00:02:00,203
Is anyone there?

10
00:02:00,286 --> 00:02:02,831
Only me,

11
00:02:02,914 --> 00:02:05,750
Oh, it's you... What do you want?

12
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:09,879
You said we'd play and fantasise,

13
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:14,676
- Have you forgotten?
- Of course... We can try.

14
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:23,143
If we're to enjoy this,
you must describe me, In detail,

15
00:02:23,226 --> 00:02:26,855
Sit down by the window,
so I can see you.

16
00:02:26,938 --> 00:02:30,191
Not until you've described me,

17
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:38,742
How shall I start?

18
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:42,495
You're very attractive.

19
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:45,165
That's a good start,

20
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:48,835
- How old am I?
- How old...?

21
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:03,892
Let me see...

22
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:10,065
You left drama school seventeen
years ago... You're about forty.

23
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:14,778
Am I an actress?
That was unexpected,

24
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:17,906
- Am I married?
- Yes.

25
00:03:17,989 --> 00:03:21,785
You're married to a conductor.
Markus.

26
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:26,748
He's enjoying
a great international career.

27
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:34,589
Otherwise I know little of
your private life - you'll have to help.

28
00:03:34,673 --> 00:03:39,052
- Any children?
- A nine-year-old daughter.

29
00:03:40,011 --> 00:03:41,930
Isabelle.

30
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:45,975
What do I look like?
Describe me,

31
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:51,439
You have a good face.

32
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:55,694
Well suited to drama and comedy.

33
00:03:56,736 --> 00:03:59,572
You can look surprised

34
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:03,410
even when you're not.

35
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:09,874
Almost unnoticeable lines
around your mouth and eyes.

36
00:04:12,377 --> 00:04:14,295
Otherwise nothing.

37
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:18,341
Are you describing Marianne?
Are you?

38
00:04:18,425 --> 00:04:21,886
It's not Marianne! I promise you.

39
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:25,140
But you need a name.
Marianne's good.

40
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:27,600
Marianne... Vogler.

41
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:31,062
"Marianne Vogler, the actress."

42
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:34,399
Now I exist?

43
00:04:34,482 --> 00:04:37,736
Come to think of it - it's a bit odd.

44
00:04:39,154 --> 00:04:44,367
A few hours ago, you didn't exist.
Nowyou're utterly real.

45
00:04:52,751 --> 00:04:57,130
- What do you want?
- Let's talk about David.

46
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:05,597
Yes...

47
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:08,641
Let's talk about David.

48
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:42,926
David and my husband
enjoyed working in opera.

49
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:49,516
David directed
and Markus conducted.

50
00:05:50,308 --> 00:05:53,019
They got on terribly well.

51
00:05:57,190 --> 00:06:01,569
David was a frequent guest
in our home.

52
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:06,908
He was married - second marriage.

53
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:14,749
It was a troubled marriage.
Two sons, six and eight.

54
00:06:14,833 --> 00:06:19,462
And what were you doing,
when it began?

55
00:06:21,172 --> 00:06:23,341
When it began...?

56
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:31,224
We were playing The Bride,

57
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:37,355
By Ostrovsky. I was the bride.

58
00:06:39,649 --> 00:06:45,030
At the time David was
out of sorts - he drank too much.

59
00:06:46,448 --> 00:06:49,617
He was working on A Dream Play,

60
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:54,914
He'd left home, was living alone.

61
00:06:59,002 --> 00:07:02,797
There were other women,
but they don't count.

62
00:07:03,923 --> 00:07:09,179
I do believe David and Markus
were real friends.

63
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:13,266
He often came to dinner.

64
00:07:14,392 --> 00:07:17,479
Isabelle loved David.

65
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:22,359
He listened

66
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:25,320
to her stories.

67
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:31,368
He swore Isabelle
had a magical personality.

68
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:38,333
They went to the cinema
and the theatre together.

69
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:44,255
And that was really it.

70
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:48,551
Nothing else...

71
00:07:49,761 --> 00:07:52,138
Are you crying?

72
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:56,226
Perhaps it's you crying?

73
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:00,689
I don't know.

74
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:07,445
Last performance ofThe Bride.

75
00:08:07,529 --> 00:08:12,450
Everyone congratulating
and embracing each other,

76
00:08:14,411 --> 00:08:19,457
All that emotional twaddle
that goes on in theatre,

77
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:24,879
We toasted with champagne
and said goodbye

78
00:08:24,963 --> 00:08:27,507
then toasted again,

79
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:32,387
When I at last got down
to the foyer, he was there,

80
00:08:33,430 --> 00:08:36,016
David,

81
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:40,603
- I'm waiting for you.
- How are you?

82
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:43,982
- You look rough.
- I'm not drunk.

83
00:08:46,985 --> 00:08:50,613
- I'm in such pain.
- Do you need a doctor?

84
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:53,116
It's not that sort of pain.

85
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:57,412
- Shall we go and get a bite to eat?
- No, thanks.

86
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:02,709
Go home and talk?
Markus is away, but still...

87
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:04,336
I'd love to.

88
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:10,216
So we took my car
and went out to ourvilla,

89
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:16,014
I said goodnight to my
indispensable Finnish nanny, Silja,

90
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:21,269
We went in to Isabelle,

91
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:27,567
She was pleased to see David
and offered to tell him a story,

92
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:38,328
I put on my dressing gown
and combed my hair,

93
00:09:39,371 --> 00:09:44,292
I made an omelette
and opened a bottle of wine,

94
00:09:44,376 --> 00:09:49,756
We chatted, David
became calmer, less edgy,

95
00:09:50,799 --> 00:09:52,884
Could you describe David?

96
00:09:57,347 --> 00:10:00,100
David is... David.

97
00:10:02,185 --> 00:10:04,813
Forty.

98
00:10:04,896 --> 00:10:07,107
Talented.

99
00:10:07,941 --> 00:10:10,068
Unpredictable.

100
00:10:13,488 --> 00:10:14,906
Kind...

101
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:18,827
Thoughtful - when he wants to be.

102
00:10:20,078 --> 00:10:25,083
Ruthless and bloody brutal
when cornered.

103
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:28,920
Not many friends.

104
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:32,757
Rather more enemies.

105
00:10:35,677 --> 00:10:38,096
Pedantically thorough.

106
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:41,224
A perfectionist in his work.

107
00:10:44,936 --> 00:10:47,897
Careless in his private life.

108
00:10:51,693 --> 00:10:56,448
I don't knowwhat to say...
We've known each other for years.

109
00:10:56,531 --> 00:10:58,950
Workmates.

110
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:03,997
There's lots to say about David.

111
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:09,961
- But my mind's a blank.
- A relationship? Excuse the question.

112
00:11:10,045 --> 00:11:13,715
Relationship? With David?

113
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:16,384
Nothing like it.

114
00:11:17,218 --> 00:11:19,137
More like siblings.

115
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:21,890
So there you were...

116
00:11:36,029 --> 00:11:39,032
David had really got going,

117
00:11:40,075 --> 00:11:43,078
He was talking about some project,

118
00:11:45,497 --> 00:11:49,376
Markus could have appeared
at any moment,

119
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:04,307
We were sleepy, both of us,
and I thought

120
00:12:04,391 --> 00:12:08,019
it might be bedtime
for brother and sister,

121
00:12:16,486 --> 00:12:18,822
I heard David

122
00:12:18,905 --> 00:12:21,074
muttering something,

123
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:23,326
Would you sleep with me?

124
00:12:24,119 --> 00:12:27,288
I heard him, but asked all the same,

125
00:12:27,831 --> 00:12:30,000
What did you say?

126
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:33,128
- He turned to me,,,
- Would you sleep with me?

127
00:12:37,257 --> 00:12:41,428
David, dearest... How do you think
that could happen?

128
00:12:48,435 --> 00:12:50,979
Thanks for the offer.

129
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:57,360
But I have to be up early, Isabelle has
school, and I have a make-up test.

130
00:13:00,447 --> 00:13:04,492
Then let's get some sleep,
in separate beds.

131
00:13:06,119 --> 00:13:09,330
In separate rooms.

132
00:13:09,414 --> 00:13:12,792
Can you lend me a toothbrush?

133
00:13:16,755 --> 00:13:19,924
I leant forward to blow out
the candles,

134
00:13:22,469 --> 00:13:26,097
and heard myself saying
something I didn't mean,

135
00:13:26,181 --> 00:13:30,560
If you want to sleep in the bedroom,
that's all right.

136
00:13:32,562 --> 00:13:35,940
If you're sad and Ionely.

137
00:13:36,024 --> 00:13:39,361
If you need to, you can hold my hand.

138
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:48,703
We got undressed,

139
00:13:49,704 --> 00:13:54,584
As ifwe were an old married couple,

140
00:13:57,170 --> 00:14:00,840
I lent David pyjamas
and a toothbrush,

141
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:06,513
I set the alarm for
an hour earlierthan usual,

142
00:14:08,014 --> 00:14:12,060
I told David
not to count on breakfast,

143
00:14:12,143 --> 00:14:15,647
He had to leave
before Isabelle woke up,

144
00:14:20,235 --> 00:14:22,821
So far so good,

145
00:14:23,697 --> 00:14:26,700
And right - or at least not wrong,

146
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:33,540
We crawled into the big bed,

147
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:38,837
I turned out the light - we were still
brother and sister, no sign of incest,

148
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:43,466
David drew

149
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:46,052
a couple of deep breaths,

150
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:52,475
I thought darkness had taken him
again, and gave him my hand,

151
00:14:52,559 --> 00:14:56,730
We fell asleep, as if
we'd always slept together,

152
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:03,570
I woke up.

153
00:15:03,653 --> 00:15:08,867
I had David's sleeping face
right up against mine.

154
00:15:13,788 --> 00:15:16,708
Then I looked at him,

155
00:15:19,419 --> 00:15:22,922
I looked at him,

156
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:30,513
I looked at him properly,

157
00:15:32,515 --> 00:15:35,018
I realised

158
00:15:36,811 --> 00:15:40,482
that I'd not seen this man before,

159
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:53,244
It was someone

160
00:15:54,704 --> 00:15:58,458
who would only exist for a second

161
00:15:58,541 --> 00:16:01,211
and never return.

162
00:16:03,171 --> 00:16:06,007
I would never see him again.

163
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:09,552
I thought...

164
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:14,516
No, "thought" is really the wrong word:

165
00:16:14,599 --> 00:16:17,018
"Thought"...

166
00:16:17,102 --> 00:16:20,230
No, I certainly wasn't thinking.

167
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:25,735
Certain senses
- that's also the wrong word.

168
00:16:28,113 --> 00:16:31,574
I was simply a part,

169
00:16:31,658 --> 00:16:35,578
a tiny part

170
00:16:35,662 --> 00:16:38,707
of something mysterious.

171
00:16:39,666 --> 00:16:43,211
These words sound so peculiar!

172
00:16:43,294 --> 00:16:46,756
I can't explain what happened.

173
00:16:47,716 --> 00:16:50,927
But it was

174
00:16:51,011 --> 00:16:54,014
something tangible...

175
00:16:55,056 --> 00:16:58,143
...that would always be there.

176
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:03,064
Inside my body,

177
00:17:04,983 --> 00:17:08,653
If you want to place it.

178
00:17:08,737 --> 00:17:11,156
Is this still just a game?

179
00:17:12,824 --> 00:17:15,827
Yes, why are we playing?

180
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:18,705
A diversion before death.

181
00:17:20,498 --> 00:17:25,128
In the remaining twilight that is left

182
00:17:26,713 --> 00:17:31,885
something happens - because of
mercilessly condensed time.

183
00:17:33,094 --> 00:17:35,680
A pull.

184
00:17:35,764 --> 00:17:38,475
A vortex.

185
00:17:38,558 --> 00:17:42,479
Forgotten emotions
beginning to move.

186
00:17:44,856 --> 00:17:50,820
I'm searching for answers
to questions I never asked.

187
00:17:52,530 --> 00:17:55,116
Frittered away deductions.

188
00:17:57,827 --> 00:18:00,622
I ask Marianne for help.

189
00:18:00,705 --> 00:18:05,210
And so we play,
making greater demands

190
00:18:05,293 --> 00:18:08,505
finding it harder to stop.

191
00:18:08,588 --> 00:18:11,466
I don't understand.

192
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:16,971
I don't understand
what you're talking about.

193
00:18:17,055 --> 00:18:19,724
I presume you want us to go on?

194
00:18:19,808 --> 00:18:21,893
Let's do that...

195
00:18:24,312 --> 00:18:27,315
Though I'm not happy with my part.

196
00:18:31,695 --> 00:18:34,072
Where shall we go from here?

197
00:18:36,032 --> 00:18:38,660
David's letter, for instance.

198
00:18:42,831 --> 00:18:45,208
David's letter.

199
00:18:48,211 --> 00:18:50,296
If you say so.

200
00:18:51,214 --> 00:18:53,925
I think I have it in my bag.

201
00:18:57,345 --> 00:18:59,639
Here it is.

202
00:19:01,141 --> 00:19:04,477
I received it the day after

203
00:19:04,561 --> 00:19:07,564
that ominous night.

204
00:19:09,441 --> 00:19:12,110
Here we go...

205
00:19:13,570 --> 00:19:18,241
"Dear Marianne. Thank you
for taking care of me."

206
00:19:18,324 --> 00:19:20,952
"It was a great help."

207
00:19:22,078 --> 00:19:25,248
"It was kind to lend me your hand."

208
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:29,461
"Your friend, David."

209
00:19:33,048 --> 00:19:35,175
That's it.

210
00:19:37,093 --> 00:19:41,598
His use of words is rather succinct.

211
00:19:41,681 --> 00:19:44,059
As for me...

212
00:19:45,477 --> 00:19:49,230
I was in a state of chaos
I can't describe.

213
00:19:51,983 --> 00:19:55,528
To be dramatic, you could say

214
00:19:56,654 --> 00:20:01,117
I'd never felt anything like it.
The question was:

215
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:06,289
Shall I keep

216
00:20:08,583 --> 00:20:11,419
all this to myself?

217
00:20:12,962 --> 00:20:15,799
Or...

218
00:20:16,841 --> 00:20:20,095
...shall I tell David?

219
00:20:20,178 --> 00:20:25,475
Keep a diary - for Isabelle to read
when I'm dead?

220
00:20:28,269 --> 00:20:32,357
The question was hypothetical.
I'd already decided.

221
00:20:33,191 --> 00:20:36,986
The warning lights were flashing,
but I'd chosen.

222
00:20:39,572 --> 00:20:43,243
Now I'm crying again.

223
00:20:44,911 --> 00:20:48,081
I have to move around.

224
00:21:04,556 --> 00:21:07,559
Your sea is lovely.

225
00:21:07,642 --> 00:21:10,770
Those pines shaped by the wind.

226
00:21:12,105 --> 00:21:15,442
That endless shoreline.

227
00:21:16,735 --> 00:21:19,779
You never see anyone here, do you?

228
00:21:25,952 --> 00:21:28,747
I'd been awarded a scholarship.

229
00:21:28,830 --> 00:21:32,083
Not a lot of money, but flattering.

230
00:21:32,667 --> 00:21:37,005
I had planned a trip to Paris,
to go to the theatres.

231
00:21:37,088 --> 00:21:41,593
Markus was going on tour to Boston,
Detroit and Los Angeles.

232
00:21:41,676 --> 00:21:43,386
Gran stayed with Isabelle.

233
00:21:43,470 --> 00:21:47,390
- Did you meet my husband?
- No, I never met Markus.

234
00:21:47,474 --> 00:21:51,353
How should I describe Markus?

235
00:21:58,526 --> 00:22:01,446
You knowwhat he looks like.

236
00:22:02,030 --> 00:22:04,824
Charming, to say the least.

237
00:22:04,908 --> 00:22:09,621
His family was Jewish,
upper middle-class.

238
00:22:10,997 --> 00:22:15,210
They were all musically talented.

239
00:22:16,127 --> 00:22:20,507
But only Markus became
a professional musician.

240
00:22:20,590 --> 00:22:25,762
He composed, conducted
and played jazz clarinet

241
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:28,473
and the piano.

242
00:22:30,350 --> 00:22:34,396
The only problem was
that he had to choose.

243
00:22:35,605 --> 00:22:38,858
He chose to conduct.

244
00:22:38,942 --> 00:22:43,196
He had a love of life.

245
00:22:46,533 --> 00:22:49,035
Joie de vivre,

246
00:22:49,119 --> 00:22:51,996
Music was,,,

247
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:55,083
,, became,

248
00:22:55,166 --> 00:22:57,210
pleasure,

249
00:23:00,213 --> 00:23:04,217
Martha, you're playing this really well,

250
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:08,763
but have you thought about
how the cello sings?

251
00:23:08,847 --> 00:23:11,474
Sing the first few bars,

252
00:23:11,558 --> 00:23:14,561
you, who sing so beautifully.

253
00:23:32,537 --> 00:23:37,792
Isabelle sits on my right,
listening intently,

254
00:23:38,918 --> 00:23:41,963
I wonderwhat she's feeling,

255
00:23:43,715 --> 00:23:46,426
My mysterious child,

256
00:23:47,552 --> 00:23:51,056
with her dreams and stories,

257
00:23:54,184 --> 00:23:57,187
She is very much Markus's child.

258
00:24:00,065 --> 00:24:03,151
They have a special relationship.

259
00:24:05,111 --> 00:24:08,073
Closed to outsiders.

260
00:24:11,868 --> 00:24:15,914
This business with David
came out of nowhere.

261
00:24:15,997 --> 00:24:19,417
I can't give you a reason.

262
00:24:24,381 --> 00:24:27,592
What madness overcame me?

263
00:24:28,843 --> 00:24:32,097
I had just one thought;

264
00:24:32,180 --> 00:24:35,225
I had to get David to Paris,

265
00:24:35,308 --> 00:24:39,145
I bumped into him
in the theatre canteen,

266
00:24:39,229 --> 00:24:45,443
I said I was going to Paris,
David barely answered,

267
00:24:45,527 --> 00:24:48,196
Noncommittal, detached,

268
00:24:50,281 --> 00:24:53,284
- Then he said;
- Let's go to the Thielska Gallery.

269
00:24:55,203 --> 00:24:58,498
- Have you been there?
- I often go.

270
00:24:59,124 --> 00:25:01,710
It's a favourite place.

271
00:25:09,009 --> 00:25:11,553
A world lost in itself,

272
00:25:11,636 --> 00:25:14,472
concealed behind thick walls.

273
00:25:14,556 --> 00:25:19,185
We ended up in the tower rooms.

274
00:25:21,312 --> 00:25:25,900
We just sat there, without speaking

275
00:25:28,361 --> 00:25:31,322
in that massive silence.

276
00:25:33,158 --> 00:25:35,910
We had nothing to say.

277
00:25:37,954 --> 00:25:40,665
Perhaps too much.

278
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:46,171
Suddenly David began
to explain himself.

279
00:25:46,254 --> 00:25:50,050
Forgive my clumsy suggestion
that evening.

280
00:25:50,133 --> 00:25:52,552
David, please...

281
00:25:53,636 --> 00:25:58,266
Nice of you to appreciate
the ridiculous side of it.

282
00:25:58,350 --> 00:26:02,687
I mess things up
for myself and others.

283
00:26:06,608 --> 00:26:10,820
I wonder if something's
seriously wrong with me.

284
00:26:12,113 --> 00:26:14,824
Perhaps I need therapy.

285
00:26:18,578 --> 00:26:22,374
I don't have a normal relationship
with reality.

286
00:26:24,584 --> 00:26:27,504
I know how it works.

287
00:26:27,587 --> 00:26:30,340
I've learnt to read people.

288
00:26:31,633 --> 00:26:36,137
But - every honest attempt at contact

289
00:26:36,221 --> 00:26:39,516
ends in failure.

290
00:26:42,644 --> 00:26:44,396
I know this.

291
00:26:45,980 --> 00:26:49,484
I ought to take
the consequences of this.

292
00:26:57,325 --> 00:27:00,161
For Christ's sake, I act the part.

293
00:27:00,787 --> 00:27:03,665
Perfectly, if I say so myself.

294
00:27:07,752 --> 00:27:09,921
Though...

295
00:27:11,464 --> 00:27:14,092
...there's always...

296
00:27:17,053 --> 00:27:21,307
...an empty second,
ifyou knowwhat I mean.

297
00:27:25,478 --> 00:27:28,606
That second is decisive.

298
00:27:30,775 --> 00:27:33,945
Then he went quiet, he just sat there.

299
00:27:36,114 --> 00:27:39,451
I had nothing to say.

300
00:27:39,534 --> 00:27:41,995
I was disorientated.

301
00:27:44,122 --> 00:27:47,417
All my plans for Paris were wiped out.

302
00:27:52,464 --> 00:27:55,300
Dusk was falling.

303
00:27:55,383 --> 00:27:57,469
It was grey.

304
00:28:01,431 --> 00:28:04,684
I leant forward and kissed David
on the lips.

305
00:28:16,988 --> 00:28:19,491
They were cold,

306
00:28:24,829 --> 00:28:27,207
This is serious.

307
00:28:29,501 --> 00:28:31,836
This is bloody serious.

308
00:28:38,968 --> 00:28:41,596
We got up together,

309
00:28:42,263 --> 00:28:48,269
We moved towards the door,,,
but we couldn't cross the threshold,

310
00:28:50,063 --> 00:28:52,649
Something had to be said.

311
00:28:56,569 --> 00:28:59,364
And anotherthing,,,

312
00:29:00,949 --> 00:29:03,743
I carry failure around.

313
00:29:05,120 --> 00:29:07,872
I don't mean occasional failures.

314
00:29:08,790 --> 00:29:11,668
My whole life's a wreck.

315
00:29:14,879 --> 00:29:18,008
Sometimes I wonder why I'm alive.

316
00:29:19,259 --> 00:29:22,971
- But suicide isn't in me.
- Another time, David.

317
00:29:23,054 --> 00:29:28,226
- Analysis can wait. Not now, please.
- I have to warn you.

318
00:29:30,854 --> 00:29:33,648
I accept you for who you are.

319
00:29:39,404 --> 00:29:43,825
If only I weren't so clumsy,
and so complicated

320
00:29:43,908 --> 00:29:46,369
beyond even comical.

321
00:29:48,246 --> 00:29:50,707
Though no one laughs.

322
00:29:50,790 --> 00:29:53,168
Least of all me.

323
00:29:56,629 --> 00:29:59,716
And then I'm suspicious.

324
00:30:03,094 --> 00:30:06,056
I don't trust anyone.

325
00:30:06,139 --> 00:30:10,435
Probably because
I lack self-confidence.

326
00:30:15,982 --> 00:30:20,362
If you like, I can go on.
No one's as rotten as I am.

327
00:30:21,571 --> 00:30:23,865
Dearest David...

328
00:30:23,948 --> 00:30:26,576
Let's look at this simply.

329
00:30:28,036 --> 00:30:30,622
It's fun,

330
00:30:35,085 --> 00:30:37,545
Yes, it's fun.

331
00:30:39,547 --> 00:30:43,802
It's simple: I've got a scholarship
and I'm going to Paris.

332
00:30:43,885 --> 00:30:48,932
It's perfect: Markus is in Los Angeles,
Isabelle with Gran.

333
00:30:51,559 --> 00:30:53,895
And you, my David...

334
00:30:55,689 --> 00:31:00,151
...happen to be going,
by a stroke of luck,

335
00:31:00,235 --> 00:31:06,241
to Paris, to meet a scenographer
or something. Everything's perfect.

336
00:31:06,908 --> 00:31:12,038
Markus will know that we're in Paris
and that we'll meet.

337
00:31:13,498 --> 00:31:17,168
No creeping around, no deceit.

338
00:31:18,253 --> 00:31:20,463
No suspicion or jealousy.

339
00:31:21,548 --> 00:31:23,800
Yes - David!

340
00:31:26,302 --> 00:31:31,141
That's how simple
and exciting it might be.

341
00:31:31,224 --> 00:31:35,353
Life needn't be a series of disasters.

342
00:31:39,357 --> 00:31:42,235
There's affection and tenderness

343
00:31:42,318 --> 00:31:45,405
and other pleasant things.

344
00:31:52,746 --> 00:31:57,125
Markus was working with
the Radio Symphony Orchestra,

345
00:31:57,208 --> 00:32:01,546
The last concert was
on a Saturday afternoon,

346
00:32:01,629 --> 00:32:06,092
We were there, of course,
David, Isabelle and I,

347
00:32:07,594 --> 00:32:09,262
Ovations,

348
00:32:43,672 --> 00:32:46,633
Afterwards, we had dinner at home,

349
00:32:47,884 --> 00:32:51,096
The atmosphere, bright and cheerful,

350
00:32:53,598 --> 00:32:56,101
We had wine

351
00:32:56,184 --> 00:32:59,312
and pralines from Zurich,

352
00:33:15,745 --> 00:33:19,416
Did Isabelle buy that bouquet?

353
00:33:22,293 --> 00:33:27,799
They've got a great programme: Six
Moliere, four Corneille and Racine.

354
00:33:27,882 --> 00:33:33,555
Phaedra; Edith Clever in a Hamburg
production. I've got to see that!

355
00:33:33,638 --> 00:33:37,058
We could see it together.

356
00:33:38,101 --> 00:33:42,230
- Are you going to Paris?
- Yes! That was a surprise.

357
00:33:42,313 --> 00:33:46,359
- I'll be in Paris from mid-June.
- That's great.

358
00:33:46,443 --> 00:33:51,614
We can go to the theatre
and have lovely meals. Fantastic!

359
00:33:51,698 --> 00:33:56,119
- And I'll be stuck in Detroit.
- Cancel your concerts!

360
00:33:56,202 --> 00:34:00,081
Say your wife and best friend
are in Paris.

361
00:34:00,165 --> 00:34:05,003
- You have to check up on them.
- What are you doing in Paris?

362
00:34:05,086 --> 00:34:10,050
I might get French-Danish-Swedish
funding for my film.

363
00:34:10,133 --> 00:34:14,220
I'm meeting Plantier and Wendtland,
among others.

364
00:34:14,304 --> 00:34:17,515
I'll have an Italian cinematographer.

365
00:34:18,683 --> 00:34:21,644
Tullio Pinera - he's in Paris,
filming with Corneau.

366
00:34:21,728 --> 00:34:26,733
He who made All the Mornings
ofthe World, Did you see that?

367
00:34:26,816 --> 00:34:29,903
He insists that we use a French lab.

368
00:34:29,986 --> 00:34:35,283
I'm not keen, nor the Danes,
who are providing the facilities.

369
00:34:35,367 --> 00:34:41,331
It's incredibly complicated. If Plantier
gets eight million, we're in business.

370
00:34:41,414 --> 00:34:47,170
The script's based on a short story
by Nicole Verdier - the core of it.

371
00:34:47,253 --> 00:34:50,465
I've set it
in turn-of-the-century Sweden.

372
00:34:50,548 --> 00:34:54,135
- Is Maria going with you?
- Maria...?

373
00:34:55,595 --> 00:34:59,641
- Oh, you mean Maria!
- Yes, your ex-wife.

374
00:35:00,934 --> 00:35:04,688
Are you joking...?
I'm meeting someone special.

375
00:35:05,730 --> 00:35:08,733
All these secrets... Whom, may I ask?

376
00:35:08,817 --> 00:35:12,153
Her name's Yvonne.

377
00:35:13,822 --> 00:35:18,034
- That's all I'm telling.
- Marianne will have to watch you.

378
00:35:18,118 --> 00:35:20,787
That'll be absolutely necessary.

379
00:35:20,870 --> 00:35:24,207
Do you speak any French?

380
00:35:35,051 --> 00:35:38,763
Let's toast to your stay in Paris.

381
00:35:38,847 --> 00:35:41,016
May it be a joy.

382
00:35:52,986 --> 00:35:55,655
Now it gets difficult.

383
00:35:56,406 --> 00:36:00,618
I have to talk about things
I'd rather not mention.

384
00:36:09,753 --> 00:36:14,007
I've told you that Markus and I
had a good sex life.

385
00:36:15,008 --> 00:36:20,347
Markus said sex with me was better
than conducting Rite ofSpring,

386
00:36:23,975 --> 00:36:25,977
Sometimes...

387
00:36:26,061 --> 00:36:28,772
Sometimes? Sometimes what?

388
00:36:28,855 --> 00:36:33,818
Sometimes when we made love,
I lost my head...

389
00:36:36,988 --> 00:36:39,366
...and my consciousness.

390
00:36:39,449 --> 00:36:43,286
Do you think it's inappropriate?

391
00:36:45,205 --> 00:36:49,793
Is it inappropriate,
me and David in Paris?

392
00:36:49,876 --> 00:36:52,587
Why should it be?

393
00:36:52,671 --> 00:36:56,007
I don't know - I thought...

394
00:36:56,091 --> 00:37:00,220
I don't really know, I just had this idea.

395
00:37:00,303 --> 00:37:03,765
Sweetheart, I'll tell you what I think.

396
00:37:03,848 --> 00:37:06,142
I just thought I'd ask.

397
00:37:06,226 --> 00:37:10,689
That my Marianne
and my David would...

398
00:37:10,772 --> 00:37:15,110
- Sometimes you're really funny.
- Why?

399
00:37:16,528 --> 00:37:19,197
David's an attractive man,

400
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:22,158
and I'm not exactly...

401
00:37:23,785 --> 00:37:25,912
You and David?

402
00:37:29,874 --> 00:37:33,044
I'll tell you why that's impossible.

403
00:37:37,298 --> 00:37:40,093
It would be treachery.

404
00:37:42,053 --> 00:37:44,639
And as I knowyou,

405
00:37:44,723 --> 00:37:47,851
at least I think I knowyou,

406
00:37:47,934 --> 00:37:51,438
and David even better, almost,

407
00:37:51,521 --> 00:37:56,985
I know there's no treachery
written into your scripts.

408
00:37:57,068 --> 00:38:00,405
- That was well put, wasn't it?
- Very.

409
00:38:07,704 --> 00:38:10,957
So I went to Paris...

410
00:38:11,041 --> 00:38:14,753
...on the second of June.
It was summer there.

411
00:38:17,380 --> 00:38:22,135
I had booked a room
at the Hotel Sainte Anne,

412
00:38:24,179 --> 00:38:27,432
An old-fashioned
English type family hotel,

413
00:38:28,141 --> 00:38:31,019
I should state this was the first time.

414
00:38:31,102 --> 00:38:35,690
- What do you mean?
- The first time I was...

415
00:38:35,774 --> 00:38:37,859
...actually unfaithful.

416
00:38:38,985 --> 00:38:41,905
A planned and staged adultery.

417
00:38:46,117 --> 00:38:48,370
It was real.

418
00:38:48,453 --> 00:38:51,873
David was coming that afternoon.

419
00:39:06,513 --> 00:39:08,723
I went for a walk

420
00:39:08,807 --> 00:39:12,102
to the Comedie Francaise,

421
00:39:12,185 --> 00:39:16,314
I picked up our tickets
for that evening's Moliere.

422
00:39:17,440 --> 00:39:21,319
I had lunch at the hotel and lay down.

423
00:40:42,817 --> 00:40:46,613
The cleanerwoke us,
to prepare the room,

424
00:40:52,285 --> 00:40:55,705
We got dressed

425
00:40:55,789 --> 00:41:00,168
and went to a restaurant
for a fantastic dinner,

426
00:41:00,251 --> 00:41:03,922
We never got to
that Moliere performance,

427
00:41:05,965 --> 00:41:10,720
That night Markus rang,
He talked about a rehearsal

428
00:41:10,804 --> 00:41:15,350
of Brahms' Violin Concerto
with Isaac Stern,

429
00:41:15,433 --> 00:41:19,938
I told him David had arrived
and we'd been to the theatre,

430
00:41:20,021 --> 00:41:25,527
Markus asked if David
was staying at the hotel, I said, yes,

431
00:41:25,610 --> 00:41:28,238
I described my lovely room,

432
00:41:28,321 --> 00:41:34,077
"Send my love to David
and give him a hug from me,"

433
00:41:34,160 --> 00:41:38,748
I yawned and said it was
nearly three in the morning,

434
00:41:38,832 --> 00:41:42,002
Markus turned serious
and said he knew that,

435
00:41:42,085 --> 00:41:44,838
Then the conversation ended

436
00:41:44,921 --> 00:41:47,882
with a fat lie,

437
00:41:51,011 --> 00:41:54,264
I put the phone down,
turned to David,,,

438
00:41:55,765 --> 00:41:58,768
,, and said Markus sends his love,

439
00:42:00,770 --> 00:42:03,940
But there was no reply,

440
00:42:04,024 --> 00:42:06,484
My lover was sleeping,

441
00:43:55,760 --> 00:43:58,680
Marianne didn't come the next day,

442
00:44:00,015 --> 00:44:02,517
Northe day after,

443
00:44:03,435 --> 00:44:08,273
I began to worry
- had I offended her?

444
00:44:08,356 --> 00:44:10,817
Bored her?

445
00:44:10,900 --> 00:44:13,820
Had we driven the "game" too far?

446
00:44:16,322 --> 00:44:19,909
I missed our meetings,

447
00:44:19,993 --> 00:44:25,290
I felt low and tried to kill
my loneliness with a book,

448
00:44:26,416 --> 00:44:28,543
On the third day, a letter came,

449
00:44:28,626 --> 00:44:30,795
Dear old director,

450
00:44:31,921 --> 00:44:36,051
I won't be coming today,
Nortomorrow,

451
00:44:37,469 --> 00:44:42,766
I don't know when I'll come, I have
a cold, and I know you hate sniffles,

452
00:44:44,517 --> 00:44:49,731
But the real reason for my absence
isn't my cold,

453
00:44:51,524 --> 00:44:56,029
It's so hard to rake overyour story,

454
00:44:58,323 --> 00:45:02,952
You sit at your desk,
looking at me attentively,,,

455
00:45:05,455 --> 00:45:09,042
,, expecting Marianne to do the work,

456
00:45:09,125 --> 00:45:13,004
Like all lousy dramatists
evade the issue by thinking

457
00:45:13,088 --> 00:45:17,759
a gifted actor can give their mess
some shape and drive,

458
00:45:21,054 --> 00:45:24,057
To be honest, I feel tormented,

459
00:45:24,140 --> 00:45:28,353
Or maybe "tormented"
is an exaggeration,

460
00:45:28,436 --> 00:45:32,565
But it's hard to talk about - love,

461
00:45:34,901 --> 00:45:40,448
That jungle of impulses
and attacks of vertigo,

462
00:45:40,532 --> 00:45:44,577
growing like a cancer,

463
00:45:45,286 --> 00:45:48,039
finally becoming impenetrable,

464
00:45:49,916 --> 00:45:54,295
I rush into situations
I'm unable to cope with,

465
00:45:56,840 --> 00:45:59,050
And I wonder,,,

466
00:46:00,176 --> 00:46:03,680
,, why I'm not worried,

467
00:46:03,763 --> 00:46:05,849
Although,,,

468
00:46:06,933 --> 00:46:09,769
,, there's one exception,

469
00:46:10,854 --> 00:46:13,690
One I can't deal with,

470
00:46:20,947 --> 00:46:23,658
I see Isabelle,,,

471
00:46:26,411 --> 00:46:29,330
I see Isabelle's little self,

472
00:46:30,874 --> 00:46:33,251
Herface,

473
00:46:35,378 --> 00:46:38,631
And then I'm frightened,

474
00:46:38,715 --> 00:46:41,426
Really frightened,

475
00:46:42,969 --> 00:46:45,972
I come to my senses,,,

476
00:46:48,016 --> 00:46:51,519
,, and think of some terrible words,

477
00:46:51,603 --> 00:46:54,731
as if written on a wall;

478
00:46:58,651 --> 00:47:01,696
What am I doing to Isabelle?

479
00:47:06,159 --> 00:47:08,995
What am I doing to Isabelle?

480
00:47:18,338 --> 00:47:22,425
Sometimes I think that
inside Marianne,,,

481
00:47:22,509 --> 00:47:25,845
- the actress I see in the mirror -

482
00:47:27,347 --> 00:47:30,350
,, inside Marianne
is anotherperson,

483
00:47:31,768 --> 00:47:34,479
with no name or identity,

484
00:47:42,654 --> 00:47:45,448
Marianne is back,

485
00:47:45,532 --> 00:47:48,034
I'm relieved,

486
00:47:48,743 --> 00:47:53,081
- So... Paris, Marianne?
- There isn't much to tell.

487
00:47:53,957 --> 00:47:56,960
We were there forthree weeks,

488
00:48:07,303 --> 00:48:09,806
Tell me about jealousy.

489
00:48:13,601 --> 00:48:16,646
One afternoon, up by Sacre-Coeur.

490
00:48:18,773 --> 00:48:21,276
The city at our feet...

491
00:48:23,445 --> 00:48:26,781
...fading in the heat haze.

492
00:48:30,493 --> 00:48:33,413
David puts his hand on my thigh.

493
00:48:35,957 --> 00:48:38,668
I grow heavy...

494
00:48:40,003 --> 00:48:44,924
...and pleasantly sleepy.
Perhaps it's time for a siesta.

495
00:48:47,052 --> 00:48:50,930
Suddenly he asks me
about my past lovers,

496
00:48:51,014 --> 00:48:57,020
He asks,,, with a smile,

497
00:48:57,103 --> 00:48:59,105
,, indifferently,

498
00:48:59,189 --> 00:49:04,235
Like engaging in foreplay
before the real activities,

499
00:49:05,487 --> 00:49:09,366
I don't sense the risk,

500
00:49:09,449 --> 00:49:12,911
I innocently tell him details of

501
00:49:12,994 --> 00:49:18,208
my modest erotic biography,

502
00:49:21,044 --> 00:49:23,880
David is asking funny,

503
00:49:23,963 --> 00:49:29,177
knowing questions,
We're both laughing,

504
00:49:30,720 --> 00:49:33,348
And I get bolder,

505
00:49:35,642 --> 00:49:38,561
Then, after dinner,

506
00:49:38,645 --> 00:49:41,606
- we'd drunk more than usual -

507
00:49:41,690 --> 00:49:44,526
that evening all hell breaks loose,

508
00:49:45,235 --> 00:49:49,239
- Can I do without this?
- Of course you can.

509
00:49:49,322 --> 00:49:54,202
For the first time in our friendship,
David scares me.

510
00:49:54,285 --> 00:49:57,038
His jealousy is mindless.

511
00:49:57,122 --> 00:49:59,833
I'm so frightened I throw up.

512
00:50:03,753 --> 00:50:06,256
I think he's going to hit me

513
00:50:07,215 --> 00:50:09,509
but he doesn't,

514
00:50:10,593 --> 00:50:13,972
What are you doing?
Let go of me!

515
00:50:17,100 --> 00:50:20,145
Are you out of your mind?

516
00:50:20,228 --> 00:50:22,522
Stop it!

517
00:50:22,605 --> 00:50:25,400
Bloody idiot!

518
00:50:52,844 --> 00:50:56,681
I'm furious...

519
00:50:58,516 --> 00:51:01,144
...but struck dumb.

520
00:51:02,604 --> 00:51:05,315
Then he's remorseful.

521
00:51:07,067 --> 00:51:09,944
Anguished.

522
00:51:11,363 --> 00:51:13,948
"Forgive me."

523
00:51:16,576 --> 00:51:20,789
I wonder if that evening
changed our relationship.

524
00:51:24,417 --> 00:51:29,214
But no... We sink deeper
into each other.

525
00:52:11,339 --> 00:52:13,800
How do we continue?

526
00:52:13,883 --> 00:52:16,136
You decide.

527
00:52:17,387 --> 00:52:18,930
I decide?

528
00:52:20,265 --> 00:52:24,060
- You decide.
- I decide.

529
00:52:27,689 --> 00:52:30,525
Our journey home.

530
00:52:33,528 --> 00:52:39,159
We'd agreed that I'd take
the morning flight,

531
00:52:39,242 --> 00:52:41,703
David the afternoon flight,

532
00:52:41,786 --> 00:52:46,750
We felt were were
up against a brick wall,

533
00:52:46,833 --> 00:52:49,878
I was miserable,

534
00:52:49,961 --> 00:52:55,717
"I know how you want
to arrange ourfuture, " he says,

535
00:52:59,346 --> 00:53:04,351
"This is what you want,
but are too cowardly to say..."

536
00:53:07,312 --> 00:53:12,359
Then he says everything
I thought but dared not say.

537
00:53:13,193 --> 00:53:14,736
Nastily.

538
00:53:14,819 --> 00:53:18,114
Outwardly, it will be as usual.

539
00:53:19,449 --> 00:53:22,369
Your marriage remains intact.

540
00:53:23,411 --> 00:53:27,123
We'll meet when it suits. Suits you,

541
00:53:27,874 --> 00:53:30,960
You want it all, and me as well.

542
00:53:31,044 --> 00:53:33,546
Is that so very silly?

543
00:53:36,257 --> 00:53:39,302
Can't we give ourselves some time?

544
00:53:42,097 --> 00:53:44,599
Can't we wait?

545
00:53:45,016 --> 00:53:47,727
See how it all goes?

546
00:53:49,562 --> 00:53:51,940
David, give us time!

547
00:53:53,316 --> 00:53:56,528
What a rotten scene we're acting.

548
00:54:37,986 --> 00:54:40,739
Many children were playing
in a house,

549
00:54:42,949 --> 00:54:45,660
The walls were red,

550
00:54:45,744 --> 00:54:50,665
and the windows were big.

551
00:54:52,208 --> 00:54:55,128
It was summer outside,

552
00:54:55,211 --> 00:54:58,381
but winter-cold.

553
00:54:58,923 --> 00:55:02,260
We wore winter clothes.

554
00:55:02,344 --> 00:55:04,596
A door opened.

555
00:55:04,679 --> 00:55:07,307
I hadn't seen that door.

556
00:55:07,974 --> 00:55:10,977
A nurse gathered two children.

557
00:55:11,686 --> 00:55:15,815
I saw a big lady inside,

558
00:55:15,899 --> 00:55:18,818
wearing my mother's fur coat,

559
00:55:18,902 --> 00:55:22,864
with a crown on her head...

560
00:55:23,990 --> 00:55:26,826
...made of gold.

561
00:55:26,910 --> 00:55:29,496
It was snowing in the room.

562
00:55:29,579 --> 00:55:32,916
I saw piles of children's clothes,

563
00:55:32,999 --> 00:55:35,627
covered with snow.

564
00:55:35,710 --> 00:55:40,548
That scared me.
I understood that the lady

565
00:55:40,632 --> 00:55:45,470
was eating one child after another.

566
00:55:46,721 --> 00:55:52,310
I realised there was no other way out,

567
00:55:52,394 --> 00:55:55,563
and I was very scared.

568
00:55:57,315 --> 00:55:59,776
Very scared.

569
00:56:23,049 --> 00:56:26,720
When we arrived in Copenhagen...

570
00:56:29,222 --> 00:56:33,768
...we heard that Stockholm airport
was closed due to fog.

571
00:56:34,853 --> 00:56:38,940
We'd have to stay at Kastrup
for several hours.

572
00:56:40,692 --> 00:56:43,486
There were hotels nearby.

573
00:56:44,821 --> 00:56:50,076
I got a cell with a shower and a TV.

574
00:56:52,495 --> 00:56:57,459
I was still miserable,
and took a tranquilizer,

575
00:56:59,377 --> 00:57:02,714
There was a knock on the door,

576
00:57:08,178 --> 00:57:10,263
It was David,

577
00:57:11,348 --> 00:57:13,683
I cried,

578
00:57:14,893 --> 00:57:17,395
I don't know why,

579
00:57:19,230 --> 00:57:22,192
We were two drowning people,

580
00:57:23,610 --> 00:57:26,613
I couldn't stop crying,

581
00:57:29,991 --> 00:57:33,328
We lay listening to the traffic,

582
00:57:33,411 --> 00:57:36,623
the planes en route,

583
00:57:37,832 --> 00:57:41,961
We held each other,
but couldn't make love,

584
00:57:42,754 --> 00:57:47,676
David's heart was thumping hard
and fast,

585
00:57:51,096 --> 00:57:53,890
He didn't sleep,

586
00:57:53,973 --> 00:57:58,228
and looked wretched
in the morning light,

587
00:57:58,311 --> 00:58:03,525
He was going to his room to shave,
but stopped in the doorway,

588
00:58:04,693 --> 00:58:07,362
I saw him standing there,,,

589
00:58:07,445 --> 00:58:10,365
His face was open,

590
00:58:11,741 --> 00:58:14,994
I'd never seen him so open,

591
00:58:15,078 --> 00:58:17,914
I've never felt such pain.

592
00:58:29,884 --> 00:58:32,470
And I thought:

593
00:58:32,554 --> 00:58:35,432
"Must it be this painful?"

594
00:58:37,225 --> 00:58:39,894
"Is this how we pay?"

595
00:59:13,553 --> 00:59:16,639
I rang David at four in the morning,

596
00:59:18,641 --> 00:59:21,353
But David didn't answer,

597
00:59:22,771 --> 00:59:25,774
The day went by,

598
00:59:25,857 --> 00:59:30,070
When we sat down to dinner,
the phone rang,

599
00:59:30,153 --> 00:59:32,989
I answered, It was David,

600
00:59:35,075 --> 00:59:38,703
I said we were eating,
He wanted to meet,

601
00:59:39,621 --> 00:59:41,956
"Can we meet at three??"

602
00:59:42,040 --> 00:59:46,961
I said I couldn't
and suggested one o'clock,

603
00:59:48,672 --> 00:59:53,718
David couldn't manage then,
and the conversation ended,

604
00:59:55,720 --> 00:59:58,682
We went on like that for several days,

605
00:59:58,765 --> 01:00:03,520
Then we gave up,
everything went silent,

606
01:00:08,191 --> 01:00:11,986
I got a letter. I'll read it.

607
01:00:15,240 --> 01:00:18,284
"I can't live like this."

608
01:00:18,368 --> 01:00:21,287
"It's humiliating."

609
01:00:21,371 --> 01:00:23,998
"Upsetting."

610
01:00:24,082 --> 01:00:26,167
"Unbearable."

611
01:00:27,460 --> 01:00:31,798
"There is one solution:
Clarity and truth."

612
01:00:32,924 --> 01:00:36,428
I went walking in the forest for hours.

613
01:00:36,511 --> 01:00:40,140
I cried - from anger, not from sorrow.

614
01:00:43,518 --> 01:00:46,604
I had some wine and wrote a reply.

615
01:00:46,688 --> 01:00:49,858
I said he'd ruined any chances
of a continuation.

616
01:00:49,941 --> 01:00:53,653
It was lucky we'd discovered
our mistake in time.

617
01:00:53,737 --> 01:00:58,616
What right had he
to give me an ultimatum?

618
01:01:00,785 --> 01:01:04,789
I told him to stay away,
in short, to go to hell,

619
01:01:04,873 --> 01:01:08,668
I posted the letter, not even
reading it through,

620
01:01:10,003 --> 01:01:12,714
It was painrelief

621
01:01:12,797 --> 01:01:15,633
after a terrible ache.

622
01:01:19,304 --> 01:01:22,766
That night Isabelle
wanted to sleep with me.

623
01:01:25,226 --> 01:01:30,398
I wonderwhat she was thinking,
She knows so much,

624
01:01:41,826 --> 01:01:44,454
Then we slept,

625
01:01:46,206 --> 01:01:50,085
I slept soundly
forthe first time since Paris,

626
01:01:54,214 --> 01:01:57,175
Normal life resumed.

627
01:01:59,636 --> 01:02:03,431
I was pleased to return to the theatre.

628
01:02:03,515 --> 01:02:06,810
I had a good part in a good play.

629
01:02:10,271 --> 01:02:12,649
Markus came home.

630
01:02:12,732 --> 01:02:15,485
He was a bit worn-out,

631
01:02:15,568 --> 01:02:18,905
But happy with his success

632
01:02:20,407 --> 01:02:23,034
and to be home,

633
01:02:23,868 --> 01:02:28,206
Markus, when in a good mood,
can be luminous,

634
01:02:54,357 --> 01:02:59,362
On August 20, the theatre re-opened.

635
01:02:59,446 --> 01:03:01,531
David and I met

636
01:03:01,614 --> 01:03:04,617
and greeted each other...

637
01:03:07,037 --> 01:03:10,498
...with a formal hug in the scrum.

638
01:03:13,168 --> 01:03:17,464
Nothing was said. In a big theatre
you don't see people

639
01:03:17,547 --> 01:03:21,509
when you're working
on different productions.

640
01:03:23,261 --> 01:03:26,514
But one afternoon

641
01:03:26,598 --> 01:03:29,976
we bumped into each other again.

642
01:03:30,060 --> 01:03:33,813
We laughed in embarrassment,
and then David asked

643
01:03:33,897 --> 01:03:39,194
if we could meet in his room
after rehearsals.

644
01:03:45,617 --> 01:03:48,661
We're heading for disaster.

645
01:03:50,747 --> 01:03:53,458
Here, I mean, at the theatre.

646
01:03:55,627 --> 01:03:58,338
A theatre disaster.

647
01:03:58,421 --> 01:04:03,802
I warned the actors we'd do
anti-theatre with A Dream Play,

648
01:04:03,885 --> 01:04:06,388
It was about time.

649
01:04:08,056 --> 01:04:10,809
Why are you so quiet?

650
01:04:12,268 --> 01:04:16,147
Can't you see I'm listening, fathead.

651
01:04:18,775 --> 01:04:21,569
Why do I always get things wrong?

652
01:04:21,653 --> 01:04:26,574
Why do I get things wrong
with the actors? With you?

653
01:04:29,786 --> 01:04:33,498
Did something change
without my realising?

654
01:04:36,251 --> 01:04:41,464
My film was postponed, then cancelled.
The row about money.

655
01:04:41,548 --> 01:04:44,467
I've got debts everywhere.

656
01:04:46,428 --> 01:04:49,139
Sometimes it's laughable.

657
01:04:56,604 --> 01:04:59,899
You were going to say something?

658
01:05:04,529 --> 01:05:05,905
Well...?

659
01:05:10,660 --> 01:05:14,789
I almost suggested that we'd meet,
but changed my mind.

660
01:05:21,087 --> 01:05:24,924
Invite me to dinner,
like in the old days.

661
01:05:26,968 --> 01:05:29,679
So I can see Isabelle...

662
01:05:31,181 --> 01:05:32,766
...and Markus.

663
01:05:57,207 --> 01:06:01,378
There was malicious talk
about David's rehearsals.

664
01:06:01,461 --> 01:06:05,340
He was rehearsing A Dream Play,
I told you that.

665
01:06:06,174 --> 01:06:09,427
I was worried

666
01:06:09,511 --> 01:06:12,764
and secretly went to see
what he was up to.

667
01:06:14,265 --> 01:06:18,603
As a child, did you hold a shell
to your ear and hear?

668
01:06:18,687 --> 01:06:21,773
I only hear

669
01:06:21,856 --> 01:06:24,442
the roar of the wind.

670
01:06:24,526 --> 01:06:28,113
I will interpret. Listen!

671
01:06:28,863 --> 01:06:32,075
The sigh of the wind

672
01:06:35,286 --> 01:06:38,665
Born beneath the clouds

673
01:06:38,748 --> 01:06:42,127
Hunted by Indra's fires

674
01:06:42,627 --> 01:06:45,046
Down on the dusty earth

675
01:06:46,172 --> 01:06:50,051
The field's litter soils our feet

676
01:06:50,135 --> 01:06:52,595
Dust of the roads

677
01:06:52,679 --> 01:06:55,140
Smoke of the cities

678
01:06:55,223 --> 01:07:00,353
Evil breaths, cooking fumes
and wine vapours

679
01:07:00,437 --> 01:07:02,731
May we endure

680
01:07:05,025 --> 01:07:08,194
On the wide sea

681
01:07:09,237 --> 01:07:11,906
We air our lungs

682
01:07:11,990 --> 01:07:14,034
Shake our wings

683
01:07:14,117 --> 01:07:16,703
And wash our feet

684
01:07:17,871 --> 01:07:22,375
I'm extremely distracted
by Johan chewing gum.

685
01:07:22,459 --> 01:07:27,297
Are you distracted?
Maestro is distracted!

686
01:07:27,380 --> 01:07:31,384
Could you leave your gum
with the stage manager?

687
01:07:31,468 --> 01:07:35,889
- How are you distracted?
- I'm simply distracted.

688
01:07:35,972 --> 01:07:38,975
It's a nicotine gum, on prescription.

689
01:07:39,059 --> 01:07:42,604
I'd rather you didn't munch on stage.

690
01:07:42,687 --> 01:07:46,066
The risk then, is simply that

691
01:07:46,149 --> 01:07:49,652
under present conditions
I'll start smoking again!

692
01:07:49,736 --> 01:07:52,030
What "conditions"?

693
01:07:52,113 --> 01:07:56,743
Didn't you know that I'm
"in a certain condition"?

694
01:07:57,410 --> 01:08:00,663
Would you please be so kind

695
01:08:00,747 --> 01:08:03,291
as to remove your gum?

696
01:08:04,250 --> 01:08:06,294
Certainly.

697
01:08:11,800 --> 01:08:15,553
Thank you, Johan.
Let's continue, Eva.

698
01:08:15,637 --> 01:08:19,015
No, I'm not going through
that shit again.

699
01:08:22,560 --> 01:08:24,771
Anyway, not today.

700
01:08:24,854 --> 01:08:27,691
Not before the premiere.

701
01:08:29,192 --> 01:08:31,861
If I may.

702
01:08:34,197 --> 01:08:37,367
If there is a premiere.

703
01:08:37,450 --> 01:08:40,203
- What do you mean?
- What he says.

704
01:08:40,286 --> 01:08:43,081
What's the point?

705
01:08:43,164 --> 01:08:48,670
David should talk to the boss.
Maybe then he'll listen to

706
01:08:48,753 --> 01:08:53,299
what we've been saying
for eight bloody weeks!

707
01:08:55,385 --> 01:08:57,554
You went to the boss?

708
01:09:03,601 --> 01:09:06,813
I thought... that only Axel...

709
01:09:07,856 --> 01:09:10,900
This conversation makes me ill.

710
01:09:10,984 --> 01:09:14,404
I'll be in my dressing room until three.

711
01:09:15,989 --> 01:09:21,161
Could I be told about
tomorrow's rehearsals.

712
01:09:25,957 --> 01:09:28,877
Isn't it just as well to call it a day?

713
01:09:29,711 --> 01:09:31,796
Right...

714
01:09:31,880 --> 01:09:33,923
Not just as well.

715
01:09:34,007 --> 01:09:36,092
It's better.

716
01:09:48,563 --> 01:09:51,649
I went straight to David's room.

717
01:09:52,817 --> 01:09:56,446
He wasn't there, but I went in.

718
01:09:58,323 --> 01:10:02,160
I didn't knowwhat I was doing.

719
01:10:02,243 --> 01:10:04,788
Or maybe I did.

720
01:10:05,747 --> 01:10:08,166
He came eventually.

721
01:10:08,249 --> 01:10:12,796
Seeing me, he waved me away:
"Not you too!"

722
01:10:14,381 --> 01:10:19,844
I went over to him and hugged him.
I said I'd be at his place in an hour.

723
01:10:19,928 --> 01:10:22,555
I left without looking back.

724
01:10:25,183 --> 01:10:28,978
Four o'clock I was standing

725
01:10:29,062 --> 01:10:31,898
outside his door, ringing the bell.

726
01:10:32,440 --> 01:10:35,068
No one opened,

727
01:10:35,151 --> 01:10:38,071
David wasn't there,

728
01:10:38,154 --> 01:10:41,616
Just as well, Better,

729
01:10:42,325 --> 01:10:46,079
I was relieved,

730
01:10:48,915 --> 01:10:51,835
I was having regrets,

731
01:10:51,918 --> 01:10:55,046
Real basic regrets,

732
01:10:56,006 --> 01:10:59,259
I was just about to leave

733
01:10:59,342 --> 01:11:02,095
when he arrived,

734
01:11:06,016 --> 01:11:10,729
I didn't ask why he was late,
He didn't say,

735
01:11:16,151 --> 01:11:18,820
It was like a dream...

736
01:11:21,239 --> 01:11:25,744
...where what you fear most
happens over and over again.

737
01:11:59,778 --> 01:12:02,906
Strange

738
01:12:02,989 --> 01:12:05,658
- not in a loving way.

739
01:12:06,368 --> 01:12:08,661
Fumbling

740
01:12:08,745 --> 01:12:10,830
and aggressive.

741
01:12:10,914 --> 01:12:15,752
David was impatient and inaccessible,
I was frightened.

742
01:12:15,835 --> 01:12:19,673
I kept thinking: I don't understand.

743
01:12:21,049 --> 01:12:23,426
I don't understand!

744
01:12:25,929 --> 01:12:28,556
We lay naked

745
01:12:28,640 --> 01:12:31,351
on the bed.

746
01:12:31,434 --> 01:12:33,561
I took his hand.

747
01:12:34,813 --> 01:12:37,440
He tried to break free, but I held on.

748
01:12:40,694 --> 01:12:43,488
No acting, please, Marianne.

749
01:12:49,411 --> 01:12:53,373
It's hopeless ifwe only
see ourselves as actors.

750
01:12:56,751 --> 01:12:59,963
You can laugh.

751
01:13:00,046 --> 01:13:02,674
Because it's all so squalid.

752
01:13:05,635 --> 01:13:07,721
Squalid?

753
01:13:10,515 --> 01:13:12,934
It's you and me, David.

754
01:13:15,645 --> 01:13:18,356
You and me,

755
01:13:25,071 --> 01:13:30,285
I knewyou were up there,
watching that wretched thing.

756
01:13:31,327 --> 01:13:34,330
Sometimes you drape yourself
in misery.

757
01:13:37,792 --> 01:13:40,503
Simple things aren't allowed
to be simple.

758
01:13:40,587 --> 01:13:44,674
Behind every reason
there's another reason.

759
01:13:49,179 --> 01:13:53,058
Is it so strange
that I felt sorry for you?

760
01:14:59,499 --> 01:15:03,503
You look as if you're wondering
how much the fuck cost.

761
01:15:06,631 --> 01:15:09,300
I'm an idiot.

762
01:15:09,384 --> 01:15:12,762
Self-awareness... or posturing?

763
01:15:15,181 --> 01:15:18,309
I mean - if a person like you...

764
01:15:19,519 --> 01:15:22,647
...feels affection for a person like me...

765
01:15:24,107 --> 01:15:27,318
...I ought to be humbly grateful.

766
01:15:28,445 --> 01:15:31,197
Instead I behave like an idiot.

767
01:15:33,742 --> 01:15:36,494
How stupid can you get?

768
01:15:37,454 --> 01:15:40,040
Turn round, and look at your idiot.

769
01:15:52,093 --> 01:15:55,180
Poor Theatre.

770
01:15:55,263 --> 01:16:00,185
There it is, carrying the load
of being a theatre.

771
01:16:02,103 --> 01:16:04,606
Poor David,

772
01:16:04,689 --> 01:16:07,650
who can't stand...

773
01:16:08,693 --> 01:16:14,032
...the conspiracy of the theatre
with the poor audience.

774
01:16:31,841 --> 01:16:34,010
What happened next?

775
01:16:35,220 --> 01:16:37,722
We settled down.

776
01:16:39,974 --> 01:16:42,644
We met twice a week...

777
01:16:44,729 --> 01:16:48,942
...in his dismal flat.
Usually after my rehearsals.

778
01:16:52,237 --> 01:16:55,448
Sometimes I suffered from
a guilty conscience.

779
01:16:55,532 --> 01:16:58,910
Or, not a guilty conscience,

780
01:16:58,993 --> 01:17:01,746
but simply grief.

781
01:17:01,830 --> 01:17:04,457
Grief?

782
01:17:04,541 --> 01:17:07,002
Yes - grief.

783
01:17:10,005 --> 01:17:14,592
Something was happening to me
that I couldn't deal with.

784
01:17:14,676 --> 01:17:17,303
Even worse...

785
01:17:17,387 --> 01:17:20,390
I knew that every day was wrong.

786
01:17:23,977 --> 01:17:26,688
But I couldn't make
a rational decision.

787
01:17:29,274 --> 01:17:32,027
It's hard. I have no words.

788
01:17:37,365 --> 01:17:40,243
I never talk about this.

789
01:17:44,914 --> 01:17:49,502
How can I talk about that
which has no words?

790
01:17:57,177 --> 01:18:00,096
A person growing into another person.

791
01:18:03,308 --> 01:18:05,518
It's inexorable.

792
01:18:06,853 --> 01:18:09,022
Frightening.

793
01:18:11,649 --> 01:18:14,486
The process can't be halted.

794
01:18:15,528 --> 01:18:18,073
It's almost biology.

795
01:18:19,532 --> 01:18:23,286
David grows into Marianne,
Marianne is frightened.

796
01:18:27,832 --> 01:18:32,253
Doesn't want to expose herself to
what she doesn't understand.

797
01:18:34,005 --> 01:18:36,841
David is different.

798
01:18:38,677 --> 01:18:43,264
He surrenders himself... recklessly,

799
01:18:44,683 --> 01:18:47,394
without reservations.

800
01:18:50,480 --> 01:18:55,276
He tells me not to feel responsible
for him. Stupid.

801
01:18:59,364 --> 01:19:03,118
Sometimes I get so tired of
his childishness.

802
01:19:05,995 --> 01:19:09,082
He has no insight...

803
01:19:10,500 --> 01:19:14,129
...or empathy. Oh, what am I saying?

804
01:19:21,594 --> 01:19:24,681
Despite all hurdles,
it was a time of kindness.
